    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-110354",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-110354"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "HAProxy 3 before 3.4.6 allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to cause a denial of service (persistent worker-thread CPU exhaustion) via an HTTP/1.1 chunked request. Although the H1 multiplexer drains the request before closing the stream, the parser repeatedly re-processes the same bytes without making progress. The affected thread stays busy at 100% CPU after timeouts expire and after the client disconnects, and repeated requests can consume all worker threads until the process is restarted.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:haproxy-0:3.4.7+git57.0faeaeda6-2.1.aarch64",
          "openSUSE Tumbleweed:haproxy-0:3.4.7+git57.0faeaeda6-2.1.ppc64le",
